# Git for Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true, which would check these out
# with CRLF line endings. bash then chokes on the shebang —
# `bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env bash^M` — and `git clone && ./install.sh`
# fails immediately, for a reason that looks nothing like the actual cause.
# Force LF on everything executed as a script, on every platform.
*.sh   text eol=lf
*.py   text eol=lf

# Markdown and config are text; let git normalise them in the repo.
*.md   text
*.json text
